From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: remote control for Linux apps

Remote desktop apps (AnyDesk, RustDesk) control the keyboard and pointer
through the RemoteDesktop portal, whose NickelOS backend asks Chrome:

- VmApplicationsService.NickelRemoteDesktopAsk(app name): asks the user
  "Allow remote control?" and, if allowed, answers with a token, creates
  the system input injector (as Chrome Remote Desktop's host does) and
  shows "<app> is controlling this device" with Stop.
- NickelRemoteDesktopInput(token, kind, source, x, y, code, down): one
  event: pointer moves (absolute in a shared screen's or window's pixels,
  or relative), buttons and keys (evdev codes, keys through
  KeycodeConverter), scrolling (pixels or wheel steps), "end". Answers
  false once the user has stopped it.

